 "result_text": "Topic nodes no longer send `grade_levels: null` (or the other five structured metadata fields), so Studio's \"must pass a list of values\" check should no longer reject them. I confirmed the module still imports, but I didn't run the tests or try an upload against Studio.\n\nThe change is in `ricecooker/classes/nodes.py`:\n- **`TreeNode.to_dict()`:** it no longer includes `grade_levels`, `resource_types`, `learning_activities`, `accessibility_categories`, `subjects` or `needs`.\n- **`ContentNode.to_dict()`:** it now includes each of those six fields only when it has a value. A content node with no grade levels set also leaves that key out of the payload, instead of sending `null`.\n\nI assumed Studio only checks these fields when the key is present. If any tests assert that `to_dict()` output contains those keys with `None`, they will now fail.",
